    "turn_idx": 45,
    "turn_text": "I read from two pieces that caught my eye and each made my daily newsletter. One was Dennis Ross, the American diplomat under the headline, I have once favored a ceasefire with Hamas, but not now. Alternatively, a view put forth by Tom Friedman most recently under the headline, please Israel, don't get lost in Hamas's tunnels. Friedman embracing much more of what I would describe as a sniper rather than shotgun approach to the situation in Gaza. You're well read. I assume you probably are dialed in on each of them. Whose approach do you most agree with that, which says this is not the time for a ceasefire or one that says Israel, you better be more measured or this is going to blow up.",
